# Test-and-Improve Loop

Use this procedure whenever asked to "test and improve", "test on <site>", or "run the improvement loop".

## Phase 1 — Sweep

Open all relevant pages as background tabs in parallel (one `new_tab` call per page). Then run `detect_boxes` on every tab in a single Python batch — one subprocess per tab, all in the same script. Print a summary table:

```
page_name   (N items)   [ERR: message if error]
  C0  control  button   cx=88  cy=113  'Add Element'
  ...
```

Flag any tab where:
- `items == 0` (nothing detected on an interactive page)
- An `error` field is present in the response
- Controls that should be present are missing (use `query` to confirm they exist in the DOM)

## Phase 2 — Functional Tests

For each flagged page and each interaction pattern to verify, run targeted tests **in parallel** where independent:

| Pattern | Test method |
|---|---|
| Click a button | `click` → `query` to confirm DOM state changed |
| Checkbox/radio | `click` → `query el.checked` |
| Type into input | `click` + `type` → `query el.value` |
| Dynamic content | `click` trigger → `wait 3s` → `detect_boxes` again |
| Right-click / context menu | `click '{"button":"right",...}'` in background with `&`, then `get_dialog` / `dismiss_dialog` |
| Drag & drop | `drag` (html5:true for HTML5 DnD) |
| File input | `set_file_input` |
| Modal close | Look for cursor:pointer elements in boxes[] or use `query` for the rect |

## Phase 3 — Classify Issues

Bucket each problem into one of three categories:

| Category | Description | Action |
|---|---|---|
| **Broken** | Command returns error / wrong result | Must fix |
| **Suboptimal** | Works but requires workaround | Should fix |
| **Limitation** | Fundamental CDP/browser constraint | Document in SKILL.md |

Common fixable issues in this codebase:
- Elements not detected by `detect_boxes` → fix `extension/page-extractor.js` (selector, area threshold, new detection pass)
- CDP serialisation error on `detect_boxes` → check if `el` reference leaks into return value
- Missing command param → add to `extension/background.js` + document in `bin/tiny-browser.mjs`

## Phase 4 — Fix

1. Edit `extension/page-extractor.js` for detection improvements
2. Edit `extension/background.js` for new/extended commands
3. Edit `bin/tiny-browser.mjs` for CLI/help catalogue
4. Edit `SKILL.md` for workflow gotchas
5. Run `npm run lint` — fix any errors before proceeding
6. Run `npm install -g .` to update the global binary
7. Restart the server: `pkill -f "node.*server.mjs"; tiny-browser &`
8. Ask the user to **reload the Chrome extension** at `chrome://extensions` (background.js and page-extractor.js changes require this)

## Phase 5 — Retest

Open **fresh tabs** (old tabs may be stale after server restart). Re-run `detect_boxes` on all previously-broken pages. Run functional tests for each fixed scenario. Confirm no regressions on previously-passing pages.

## Phase 6 — Commit

```bash
cd /Users/adam.pavlat/projects/personal/tiny-browser-mcp
git add -A
git commit -m "fix: <summary of what was fixed>"
git push
```

## Key file locations

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `extension/page-extractor.js` | DOM element detection logic |
| `extension/background.js` | CDP command handlers |
| `bin/tiny-browser.mjs` | CLI entry point + COMMANDS catalogue |
| `bin/server.mjs` | HTTP/WS server, AUTO_SCREENSHOT, AUTO_DETECT sets |
| `SKILL.md` | Agent workflow docs and gotchas |

## Parallelism notes

- Always open multiple tabs in a single Python script (faster than sequential shell calls)
- Run `detect_boxes` on all tabs in one Python batch
- Independent functional tests can run in the same shell command via `&&` chaining
- Never loop over tab IDs in bash — use Python for dynamic data
